  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PatDisc_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "In the clinic waiting room, you start flipping through a brochure about
    cancer research. You\u2019re surprised at how involved patients seem to be throughout
    the entire research process, and you mention this to your friend sitting next
    to you. He responds, \u201CI\u2019m pretty sure patients don\u2019t play a role
    in research until the clinical trials begin.\u201D\nIs this True or False?"
  explanation: Even before clinical trials start, patients play an important role
    in shaping research. While they are not yet participants in this stage, patients
    are informants, contributors, and guides. Their medical data, donated biospecimens,
    advocacy, and lived experiences help researchers choose what to study, explain
    why it matters, and design studies in ways that can truly benefit patients later
    on.
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
